#230
//// File ////

Loads an ICF (Icom Cloning Format) file, saves the current
file, deletes a file, activates a DOS command interpreter,
or quits this program.

When saving an ICF file, any cloning comment specified in
the Common screen is also saved in the file for further
reference.
#231P
//// Screen ////

Sets transceiver data in several screens.
Open a screen, then set data.


In addition, once a screen is opened, the following method
is available to select other screens:

     Push [SHIFT] + [Page Up]
       or [SHIFT] + [Page Dn]


* NOTE
1.An optional UT-96 is necessary to use the
  settings in the RX Code CH screen.

2.Wide/Narrow selection

  Each channel can be set to wide/narrow for both receive
   IF bandwidth and transmitter modulation.  Note that
   this capability is not available for some versions.

  Push [Backspace] to select bandwidth when Rx frequency
   is entered.
   * "n" appears between Rx frequency and Tx frequency,
     when the narrow width is selected.

   RELATED SETTING
   ------------+-----------------------------------------------
   Wide/Narrow | Key Assign screen.
   ------------+-----------------------------------------------

3.An optional UT-105 is necessary to use the SmarTrunk mode.
  Set MR-CH Bank/Free to Bank in the Key & Display Assign screen
  before setting the channel attribute in the Memory Channel screen.
  SmarTrunk mode can be selected for each bank.
  "SmarTrunk (or SmTr)" appears at the left side of the screen, when
  SmarTrunk mode is selected.

4.An optional UT-109(#02) or UT-110(#02) Voice Scrambler unit is necessary
  to use the voice scrambler function.
  Set [Scrambler] in the Key & Display Assign screen.
  UT-109(#01) and UT-110(#01) are designed for IC-F3/S series. Make sure
  the unit's version(#) number before installation.
#231L
//// Screen ////

Sets transceiver data in several screens.
Open a screen, then set the data.


In addition, once a screen is opened, the following method
is available to select other screens:

     Push [SHIFT] + [Page Up]
       or [SHIFT] + [Page Dn]


* NOTE
1.An optional UT-96 is necessary to use the settings in the RX
  Code CH screen.

2.Wide/Narrow selection

  Each channel can be set to wide/narrow for both receive
   IF bandwidth and transmitter modulation.  Note that
   this capability is not available for some versions.

  Push [Backspace] to select bandwidth when Rx frequency
   is entered.
   * "n" appears between Rx frequency and Tx frequency,
     when the narrow width is selected.

   RELATED SETTING
   ------------+-----------------------------------------------
   Wide/Narrow | Key Assign screen.
   ------------+-----------------------------------------------

3.An optional UT-105 is necessary to use the SmarTrunk mode.
  Set MR-CH Bank/Free to Bank in the Key & Display Assign screen
  before setting the channel attribute in the Memory Channel screen.
  SmarTrunk mode can be selected for each bank.
  "SmarTrunk (or SmTr)" appears at the left side of the screen, when
  SmarTrunk mode is selected.

4.An optional UT-109(#02) or UT-110(#02) Voice Scrambler unit is necessary
  to use the voice scrambler function.
  Set [Scrambler] in the Key & Display Assign screen.
  UT-109(#01) and UT-110(#01) are designed for IC-F3/S series. Make sure
  the unit's version(#) number before installation.
#232
//// Clone ////

Connect the transceiver with the following cloning cables:

     OPC-478 + OPC-592

For reading or writing data between the transceiver and PC.


"Information" allows you to read the connected transceiver
type, installed option(s) as well as any programmed comments
(set in the Common screen), etc.
#233
//// Print ////

Prints the current screen data or all screen data.
#234
//// Model ////

Selects the transceiver model.
 LMR
 PMR


"Model" is automatically selected during clone read or file
load, therefore, this selection is not usually necessary.

However, it can be helpful when you want to change the model
(version) while retaining the same frequencies and some
other settings.
#235
//// Setup ////

Sets the display type and selects an RS-232C port.

Color is recommended for a color CRT display and monochrome
1/2 is recommended for a monochrome LCD display.
#158P
//// Channel Attribute ////

-----------+------------------------------------------------
Priority   |[] One push selection with the [PRI A]
channel A  |   or [PRI A(Rewrite)] key.
           |[] Automatic selection with the hanger function.
           |[] Monitored during priority scan.
           |[] Priority channel A can be reassigned by
           |   pushing the [PRI A(Rewrite)] key for 1 sec.
-----------+------------------------------------------------
Priority   | One push selection with the [PRI B] key.
channel B  |
-----------+------------------------------------------------
Emergency  | Emergency transmission channel with the
channel    | [Emergency Single] or [Emergency Repeat] key.
-----------+------------------------------------------------
Emergency  | When there is no emergency channel, emergency
channel OFF| transmission is performed on the operating
           | channel.
-----------+------------------------------------------------
SmarTrunk  | Push the [Enter] key to toggle the SmarTrunk
ON/OFF*    | function ON/OFF.
-----------+------------------------------------------------
Channel    | Inserts a line space at the cursor position.
insert     |
-----------+------------------------------------------------
Channel    | deletes the line at the cursor position.
delete     |
-----------+------------------------------------------------

* NOTE
1:Set MR-CH Bank/Free to Bank in the Key & Display Assign screen
  before setting the channel attribute in the Memory Channel screen.
  SmarTrunk mode can be selected for each Bank.
  "SmarTrunk (or SmTr)" appears at the left side of the screen, when
  SmarTrunk mode is selected.

2:When turning SmarTrunk mode ON, set all functions which will not be
  used for trunking operations OFF.
  Otherwise, the SmarTrunk system will not function properly.




RELATED SETTINGS:
--------------------+---------------------------------------
[PRI A], [PRI B]    |  Key assignment in the
[Emergency Single]  |  Key & Display Assign screen
[Emergency Repeat]  |
--------------------+---------------------------------------
Hanger function     |  Key & Display Assign screen
--------------------+---------------------------------------
Priority scan       |  Scan List screen
--------------------+---------------------------------------
Emergency function  |  Expert screen
 (detailed settings)|
--------------------+---------------------------------------
Emergency cancel    |  RX Code CH screen
--------------------+---------------------------------------
