#003
//// CTCSS/DTCS ////

For CTCSS frequency selection:

[] Push [Enter] to indicate the frequency list window,
   then make a selection.

[] Directly input the tone frequency.
   (Input a decimal, otherwise, a DTCS code is selected.)

[] Use [Space] or [Backspace] to increase or decrease the
   frequency respectively.




For DTCS selection:

[] Enter the desired 3-digit code number directly.
     N: for normal polarity,  I: for Inverse polarity

[] Push [Space] or [Backspace] to toggle the polarity.

[] When the [C.Tone CH Ent] key is assigned to the
   transceiver, the C. Tone memory has priority than
   this setting.




NOTES:

  []  "<-" indicates the same frequencies are used for both
      the tone encoder and decoder.

  []  See one of the document files for usable DTCS codes.



RELATED SETTINGS:
---------------------------+--------------------------------
CTCSS reverse burst        | Common screen (lower left)
---------------------------+--------------------------------
RX AF switch(Low cut)      | Common screen (middle left)
---------------------------+--------------------------------
#005L
//// Text ////

Appears when the operating channel is selected.

When no text is programmed, channel number appears.


       ** USABLE CHARACTERS                      **
       **                                        **
       **     A to Z (upper- and lowercase)      **
       **     0 to 9                             **
       **     $ % ' ( ) * + , - / < = > ? @      **
       **     [ \ ] ^ _ ` { | } ~                **
       **                                        **
       **     ":" = transmit mark (upper arrow)  **
       **     ";" = receive mark  (lower arrow)  **
       **                                        **

* NOTE
1:Some lowercase letters may be difficult to read on the transceiver's
  display.

2:To eliminate display flickering in SmarTrunk mode, use the same text for
  channels with the same bank number.

3:The programmable character generator's character can not be used for the
  1st and 2nd text letters. (See Expert screen; Character Editor)
  In such cases no character appears in the above positions.
#005P
//// Text ////

Appears briefly or permanently when the operating channel is
selected.

When no text is programmed, channel number appears.


       ** USABLE CHARACTERS                      **
       **                                        **
       **     A to Z (upper- and lowercase)      **
       **     0 to 9                             **
       **     $ % ' ( ) * + , - / < = > ? @      **
       **     [ \ ] ^ _ ` { | } ~                **
       **     ":" = transmit mark (upper arrow)  **
       **     ";" = receive mark  (lower arrow)  **
       **                                        **

* NOTE
1:Some lowercase letters may be difficult to read on the transceiver's
  display.

2:To eliminate display flickering in SmarTrunk mode, use the same text
  for channels with the same bank number.

3:The programmable character generator's character can not be used for
  the 1st and 2nd text letters. (See Expert screen; Character Editor)
  In such cases no character appears in the above positions.
