#008P
//// Lockout ////

This function restricts transmission as follows:
----------+------------------------------------------------------
OFF       | No restriction for receiving signal.
----------+------------------------------------------------------
Busy      | Transmission is inhibited while receiving a
          | signal.
----------+------------------------------------------------------
Repeater  | Transmission is permitted only while:
  (1)     |   [] receiving a matched CTCSS (or DTCS)
          |   [] receiving no signal
----------+------------------------------------------------------
Repeater  | "Audible" mode :
  (2)     |  ş the same as Repeater 1 above.
          |
(reverse  | "Inaudible" mode :
 repeater |  ş transmission is permitted only while receiving an
 lockout) |    unmatched CTCSS ( or DTCS).
----------+------------------------------------------------------






RELATED SETTINGS:
----------------------+-------------------------------------
Lockout penalty timer |  Common screen (lower left)
----------------------+-------------------------------------
#008L
//// Lockout ////

This function restricts transmission under the following
conditions:
----------+-------------------------------------------------
OFF       | No restriction for receiving signal.
----------+-------------------------------------------------
Busy      | Transmission is inhibited while receiving a
          | signal.
----------+-------------------------------------------------
Repeater  | Transmission is permitted only while:
          |   [] receiving a matched CTCSS (or DTCS)
          |   [] receiving no signal
----------+-------------------------------------------------


RELATED SETTINGS:
----------------------+-------------------------------------
Lockout penalty timer |  Common screen (lower left)
----------------------+-------------------------------------
#159
//// Scan ////

This item assigns scan list number(s) to a selected channel.
Channels in scan lists align vertically in the column.

In addition, the [Scan add/del (Tag)] key modifies the
assignment from the transceiver front panel.  This item
includes inhibition of such modification.



SELECTION METHOD:

  [] Push [1] to [5] to toggle the
     selection.
     The indicated number is assigned scan list number.

  [] Push [Backspace] to toggle scan list modification
       "inhibit" (bracket appears)
       "Enable"  (bracket disappears)


RELATED SETTINGS:
------------------------+-----------------------------------
Type of scan            | Scan List screen
 and its condition      |
------------------------+-----------------------------------
Hanger action (Scan)    | Key & Display Assign screen
------------------------+-----------------------------------
Power ON scan           | Scan List screen
------------------------+-----------------------------------
#009
//// SW Action Moni ////

------------+-----------------------------------------------
OFF         | [] No function during "Inaudible" mode.
            | [] Push and hold to open any mute condition.
------------+-----------------------------------------------
Audible     | [] Push to select "Audible" mode.
            | [] Push and hold to open any mute condition.
------------+-----------------------------------------------
Inaudible   | [] Select "Inaudible" mode.
------------+-----------------------------------------------
Inaudible + | [] Select "Inaudible" mode.
 Reset 1(32)| [] Transmits reset code (see below)
    or      |
Inaudible + |
 Reset 2(31)|
------------+-----------------------------------------------
Both        | [] Push to toggle between "Inaudible" and
            |    "Audible".
            | [] Push and hold to open any mute condition.
------------+-----------------------------------------------
Both +      | [] Push to toggle between "Inaudible" and
 Reset 1(32)|    "Audible".
    or      | [] Push and hold to open any mute condition.
Both +      | [] Transmits reset code (see below)
 Reset 2(31)|
------------+-----------------------------------------------

Reset code  : Transmit Tx code channel 32 (for reset code 1)
              or 31 (for reset code 2) when switching from
              "Audible" to "Inaudible" by the [Moni] key to
              set the other station to "Inaudible" mode.




