#015
//// Channel Mute ////

This item selects:
1) Receive 5-tone mute is turned ON or OFF.
2) PTT transmission is inhibited in "Inaudible" mode.

-----------+------------------------------------------------
Continuous | 5-tone mute is OFF / PTT mute is OFF
           | (CTCSS or DTCS is usable for receive mute.)
-----------+------------------------------------------------
Single     | 5-tone mute is ON / PTT mute is ON
           | (CTCSS or DTCS can be used together with 5-tone
           |  mute.)
-----------+------------------------------------------------


NOTES:

[] To use 5-tone mute ("Single" selection), the optional
   UT-96 5-tone decoder unit is necessary.

[] 5-tone decoder is activated for operation in the RX Code
   CH screen even when "Continuous" is selected in this
   item.



RELATED SETTINGS:    All of the settings in this program.
#016
//// 5-tone Signaling Form ////

Selects the 5-tone format. A user tone can be specified in
the USER TONE screen.
#017
//// 5-tone Signaling RPT/STN/ID ////

When the [Call] key is pushed, the following 5-tone codes
are transmitted in sequence.  These columns specify the
TX code channel number used.


RPT : Repeater code
                    -+
STN : Station code   |  Sequence of these codes can be
ID  : ID code        |  changed in "ID Pos" column.
                    -+


SELECTION METHOD:

(1) Set the TX code contents in the TX Code CH screen in
    advance.

(2) Assign a TX code channel number to these codes.
     * Enter "0" to turn OFF the specified code.

(3) Push [Space] or [Backspace] to turn the long tone ON and
    OFF.
     * "L" appears when the long tone is turned ON.



NOTES:

[] When STN (station) is turned OFF, the [Call] key does not
   function.

[] ID code can be turned OFF in the next column, "ID Pos".
   If ID code is turned OFF in this column, "Log IN/OFF"
   and "TOT ID" function cannot be used.



RELATED SETTINGS:
-----------------------+------------------------------------
Contents of 5-tone code| TX Code CH screen
-----------------------+------------------------------------
[Call] key assignment  | Key & Display Assign screen
-----------------------+------------------------------------
[TX Code CH up/down],  |Key & Display Assign screen
or [Tx Code] key       |
assignment.            |
 (for station code)    |
-----------------------+------------------------------------
PTT call at inaudible  | TX Code CH screen (lower right)
                       |  *[PTT] activates for the Call key
-----------------------+------------------------------------
Auto CH call           | Scan List screen
                       |  * Call transmission on a non-busy
                       |    channel.
-----------------------+------------------------------------
#020
//// 5-tone Signaling POS //// (ID position)

Sets the sequence of the 5-tone code.

In addition, the 5-tone decoder (in RX Code CH) screen
detects the station code (mute release) and ID code (for
indication) in this sequence.
#021
//// RX C-No //// (Receive 5-tone code)

Each RX Code channel has some functions, such as answer
back, beep, indication, etc., when a matched 5-tone code
(station code) is received.

This column assigns the RX Code channel to the operating
channel.  Up to 8 kinds of channel numbers can be assigned.
The group code channel is assigned regardless of this
column's settings.



SELECTION METHOD:
  Push [1] to [8] to toggle the selection.
   *Indicated channels are effective
    Non-indicated channels are not effective.



RELATED SETTINGS:
--------------------+---------------------------------------
Contents of RX code | RX Code CH screen
--------------------+---------------------------------------
[ID-MR] select key  | Key & Display Assign screen
--------------------+---------------------------------------
#025
//// 2-tone Code ////

Turns ON the 2-tone receive mute and specifies the RX code
channel to the operating channel.

To turn OFF the setting, enter "0".


NOTE: An optional unit UT-96 is necessary for 2-tone mute function.



RELATED SETTINGS:
------------------------+-----------------------------------
Contents of 2-tone code | RX Code CH screen
------------------------+-----------------------------------
[Moni] key assignment   | Key & Display Assign screen
                        | for releasing the 2-tone mute.
------------------------+-----------------------------------
Hanger function (Moni)  | Key & Display Assign screen
------------------------+-----------------------------------
#022
//// Scrambler ON/OFF/INH ////

Turns the scrambler function "ON" or "OFF" as a initial setting.
This item can also be turned "ON" or "OFF" with a program function switch
when the function is assigned to a switch.
"INH" : This means the scrambler function selection is inhibited.
Optional UT-109(#02) or UT-110(#02) Voice Scrambler unit is required.
#023
//// Scrambler code ////

Set the scrambler code number.
Selectable value;
    UT-109: 1 to 32
    UT-110: 1 to 255
* Set the scrambler group code in the Common screen in advance.
  (UT-110 only)
