#049P
//// Hanger Action ////

Several functions are available for the hanger function when
taking the microphone from its hanger (hanger-off) and/or
returning it to the hanger (hanger-on).

-------+---------------------------------------------------
Moni   | [] Selects "Audible" at hanger-off
       | [] Selects "Inaudible" at hanger-on
       | (according to the "SW Action Moni" column in the
       |  Memory CH screen.)
-------+---------------------------------------------------
Scan   | Starts scan at hanger-on.
-------+---------------------------------------------------
Prio A | Selects priority A channel at hanger-off.
-------+---------------------------------------------------
#049L
//// Hanger Action ////

Several functions are available for the hanger function when
taking the microphone from its hanger (hanger-off) and/or
returning it to the hanger (hanger-on).

-------+---------------------------------------------------
Moni   | [] Turns the CTCSS or DTCS OFF at hanger-off
       | [] Turns the CTCSS or DTCS ON at hanger-on
-------+---------------------------------------------------
Scan   | Starts scan at hanger-on.
-------+---------------------------------------------------
Prio A | Selects priority A channel at hanger-off.
-------+---------------------------------------------------
#051
//// Beep ON/OFF ////

The confirmation beeps can be turned ON and OFF.

Note that some beeps, such as for the lockout timer, cannot
be turned OFF.

NOTE: The beep level can be preset to turn the trimmer volume in the
Mic connector on the front panel.
This setting affects the 5-tone/DTMF encoder monitor level and
caution beeps, such as the TOT beep.
#052
//// Light ////

Push to select the backlight condition.
 ON  : Turns ON the backlight continuously.
 OFF : Turns OFF the backlight.
 AUTO: Turns ON/OFF depends on the ACC socket pin 1 voltage.
       ON: low(0 V), OFF: high(12 V)
#053
//// RF Power Selection ////

-------------+----------------------------------------------
MR CH        | Output power keys, [High], [Low1] and [Low2],
 individual  | select power temporarily.
             | Returns to the previous power when changing
             | the channel.
-------------+----------------------------------------------
Override     | [] Output power keys select the power
             |    permanently.
-------------+----------------------------------------------



