#054
//// M-CH Bank/Free ////

This item selects the channel separation style, "Bank" type
or "Non-bank" (Free) type.

When "Bank" type is selected, the following number of banks
are available:
  []  2 banks for the  32 ch models


NOTE: When selecting the "Bank" type, one of the
[Bank] keys must be assigned to the transceiver.
#056
//// Opening Text ////

This set text appears for 2 sec. when turning the
transceiver ON.

To turn power ON without text indication, set this item to
blank.

       ** USABLE CHARACTERS                      **
       **                                        **
       **     A to Z (upper- and lowercase)      **
       **     0 to 9                             **
       **     $ % ' ( ) * + , - / < = > ? @      **
       **     [ \ ] ^ _ ` { | } ~                **
       **     ":" = transmit mark (upper arrow)  **
       **     ";" = receive mark  (lower arrow)  **
       **                                        **

NOTE:
1.Some lowercase letters may be difficult to read on the transceiver's
  display.

2.The programmable character generator's character can not be used for
  the 1st and 2nd text letters. (See Expert screen; Character Editor)
  In such cases no character appears in the above positions.
#057
//// MR/Code Display ////

Selects the indication text (or channel number).
-----------+------------------------------------------------
MR CH      | Operating channel's text (or channel number
           | when text is not programmed).
-----------+------------------------------------------------
TX code CH | TX Code channel's text (or code digits when
           | text is not programmed).
-----------+------------------------------------------------
MR CH +    | Operating channel number and 5 letters of TX
TX code CH | Code channel's text (or 5 digits of code
           | contents when text is not programmed).
-----------+------------------------------------------------


NOTES:

[] When "TX Code CH" or "MR CH + TX Code CH" is selected,
   operating channel appears briefly when selecting a
   channel.

[] When "MR CH + TX Code CH" is selected
   spaces in the left side are removed for maximum digit
   indication.
#060P
//// DTMF Code Channels ////

[] The programmed DTMF codes are transmitted when the [DTMF]
   key is pushed and held.

[] 7 DTMF channels can be selected by:
     pushing [DTMF] momentarily, then pushing [CH Up] or
     [CH Dn].
#060L
//// DTMF Code Channels ////

[] The programmed DTMF codes are transmitted when the [DTMF]
   key is pushed and held.

[] 7 DTMF channels can be selected by:
     pushing [DTMF] momentarily, then pushing [CH Up] or
     [CH Dn].

  (Channels "Emergency" and "Log/ID" can be used as channels
   6 and 7 respectively.)
#061
//// DTMF Timer ////

Sets the tone period for each code emission and interval.
#062
//// 1st Timer ////

Sets the tone period for the 1st DTMF code
corresponding to a scanning transceiver
or the power saver function of a portable transceiver.
#063
//// [*] [#] Timer ////

Sets the tone period for [*] (same as "E") and [#] (same as
"F").

These codes may be used for control codes depending on
signaling system.


* NOTE: When these special codes are used for the 1st code,
       the "1st Timer" has priority over this setting.
#156
//// Continuous Tone ////

The programmed continuous tone is used for encoder and/or
decoder.

Push the [C.Tone CH Ent] key, then push a [UP]/[DOWN] key
(continuous tone memory channel number) to selects the tone.


In addition, pushing [C.Tone CH Ent] then [Tone-M] selects the
channel independent tone (programmed in the Memory CH screen).
#222
//// Scan Mode List ////

---------+--------------------------------------------------
Scan OFF | Deactivates the selected list.  The list cannot
         | be selected from the transceiver front panel.
---------+--------------------------------------------------
Mode 1   | Scan proceeds in sequence from lower to higher
(Normal) | channel numbers.
---------+--------------------------------------------------
Mode 2   | Busy channel selection when scan is canceled.
(Prio A) | [] Scan proceeds in sequence while checking
         |    priority A channel.
         | [] When scan is canceled during signal reception
         |    the paused channel is retained.
---------+--------------------------------------------------
Mode 3   |Priority channel selection when scan is canceled.
(Prio A) | [] Scan proceeds in sequence while checking
         |    priority A channel.
         | [] When scan is canceled during signal reception
         |    the priority A channel is selected.
---------+--------------------------------------------------


