#225
//// Stop Timer ////

This setting is effective only when a priority scan, Mode-2
or Mode-3, is selected.

When the priority scan is paused on a busy channel, the scan
becomes priority watch to check the priority A channel.
This item sets the period paused on a busy channel (watching
interval).
#226
//// Resume Timer ////

Scan pauses on a busy channel and resumes when the signal
disappears.

This item sets the period from when the signal disappears to
when the scan resumes.
#227
//// Power ON Scan ////

The scan function is started automatically when the
transceiver power is turned ON.

NOTE: The scan function is activated only when the
      microphone is placed on the its hanger.


The hanger function (Scan) in the Key & Display Assign
screen should be turned ON when using the "Power ON Scan"
function.
#228
//// Auto Channel Call ////

When pushing the [Call] key:
[] The transceiver starts scan, then
[] detects an empty channel (non-busy channel), then
[] transmits the 5-tone codes.



NOTES:

[] The previously transmitted 'station code' is used in the
   5-tone encoder sequence.

[] An empty channel is detected from the selected scan list.

[] [Call A] and [Call B] keys have no relation with this
   function.
#030
//// RX Freq(Hz) 1st and 2nd ////

[] When UT-96 is installed:
Sets the receive 1st and 2nd tone frequencies from 250 to
3300 Hz (nearest available frequency is selected).
#HrxfG
//// RX Freq for Group Call Channel ////

Tone frequencies cannot be set since the same tones are used
for other channels.  Group call is detected for tone length
according to the following "Group Timer" item.
#032
//// Group Call ////

Specifies which tones, 1st or 2nd, are used for the group
code.
#033
//// Text ////

The set text appears when a matched 2-tone code is received.


       ** USABLE CHARACTERS                      **
       **                                        **
       **     A to Z (upper- and lowercase)      **
       **     0 to 9                             **
       **     $ % ' ( ) * + , - / < = > ? @      **
       **     [ \ ] ^ _ ` { | } ~                **
       **     ":" = transmit mark (upper arrow)  **
       **     ";" = receive mark  (lower arrow)  **
       **                                        **

NOTE:
1.Some lowercase letters may be difficult to read on the
        transceiver's display.

2.The programmable character generator's character can not be used for
  the 1st and 2nd text letters. (See Expert screen; Character Editor)
  In such cases no character appears in the above positions.
#084L
//// Bell ////

Selects the bell indicator condition when receiving a
matched 2-tone.

------+-----------------------------------------------------
Null  | The bell indicator condition is not changed even
      | when a matched code is received.
------+-----------------------------------------------------
OFF   | The bell indicator goes off.
------+-----------------------------------------------------
ON    | The bell indicator appears until operating a key.
------+-----------------------------------------------------
Blink | The bell indicator blinks until operating a key.
------+-----------------------------------------------------
#034L
//// Answer Back ////

Turns the answer back function ON and OFF.

The function transmits 1 kHz single tone for 2 sec. when
receiving a matched 2-tone.
#087L
//// External Output ////

An optional cable, OPC-617 and external connection is
necessary.

Activates an external buzzer, horn honk, etc., when
receiving a matched 2-tone.

The activation time can be set in the EXO timer item below.
#088L
//// Beep ////

Emits (or turns OFF) the following beeps when receiving a
matched 2-tone.
-------------+----------------------------------------------
Null         | Beep emission (or non emission) is retained
             | even when receiving a matched 2-tone.
-------------+----------------------------------------------
OFF          | Repeated beep emission is turned OFF.
-------------+----------------------------------------------
Pi   (single)| 1 high beep once.
-------------+----------------------------------------------
PiPi (single)| 2 high beeps once.
-------------+----------------------------------------------
PiRo (single)| 1 high and 1 low beep 3 times.
-------------+----------------------------------------------
Pi   (repeat)| 1 high beep repeated at the selected
             | intervals.
-------------+----------------------------------------------
PiPi (repeat)| 2 high beeps repeated at the selected
             | intervals.
-------------+----------------------------------------------
PiRo (repeat)| 1 high, 1 low beep 3 times, repeated at
             | the selected intervals.
-------------+----------------------------------------------
#089L
//// Auto Transmit ////

Sets the transceiver to the transmit condition (by
activating the microphone) when receiving a matched 2-tone.

This transmit time can be set in the auto TX timer item
below.
#091L
//// Stun ////

Sets the transceiver to following condition when receiving a
matched 2-tone.
-----+------------------------------------------------------
OFF  | The transceiver can be used continuously.
-----+------------------------------------------------------
Kill | The transceiver cannot be used.
     | Cloning is necessary to activate the transceiver.
-----+------------------------------------------------------
Stun | User password prompt appears.
     | When user does not know the password, the transceiver
     | cannot be used.
-----+------------------------------------------------------



RELATED SETTINGS:
----------------+-------------------------------------------
User password   | Common screen (upper left)
----------------+-------------------------------------------
PWR ON password | Common screen (upper right)
                |  *Password input is necessary regardless
                |   of this setting.
----------------+-------------------------------------------
#092L
//// Scan ////

Selects the following scan condition when receiving a
matched 2-tone:
--------+---------------------------------------------------
Null    | Scan condition is unaffected.
--------+---------------------------------------------------
Cancel  | Cancels the scan.
--------+---------------------------------------------------
Start   | Starts the scan.
--------+---------------------------------------------------


RELATED SETTINGS:
-----------------------+------------------------------------
Power ON scan          | Scan List screen
-----------------------+------------------------------------
Hanger function (Scan) | Key & Display Assign screen
-----------------------+------------------------------------
#099
//// Notone Timer ////

This item sets the acceptable period between 2 tones.

When received tones are interrupted for longer than this
setting, the transceiver does not detect the code.
#100
//// Group Timer ////

This item sets the 2-tone decoding period.

When the received tone is longer than this setting, the
transceiver detects the tone as a group code.
#096L
//// External Output Timer ////

When the EXO function is turned ON, the EXO terminal of the
optional ACC cable is grounded for this period when
receiving a matched 2-tone.
#097L
//// Beep Repeat Timer ////

When "Repeat" is selected in the "Beep" column above, beeps
are repeated at this set interval.
#098L
//// Auto TX Timer ////

When the Auto TX function is turned ON, the transceiver
transmits for this set period when receiving a matched
2-tone.
#035
//// Code Type ////

This item selects "individual code" type or "Group code" type.
#036
//// 1st Tone Frequency ////

Sets the transmit 1st frequencies from 250 to 3300 Hz
(nearest available frequency is selected).
#037
//// 1st Tone Period ////

Sets the tone period for the 1st tone code.
#038
//// 2nd Tone Frequency ////

Sets the transmit 2nd frequencies from 250 to 3300 Hz
(nearest available frequency is selected).
#039
//// 2nd Tone Period ////

Sets the tone period for the 2nd tone code.
#082
//// RX Code ////

Prepare RX 5-tone codes for assignment to each operating
channel.

Up to 7 digits can be programmed.


[] STATUS FUNCTION
When inputting "+" instead of number(s), the digits are used
for the status function, which indicates a number message.

Any number is accepted for decoding and is indicated on the
display instead of programmed text or decoded ID when
receiving the call.
#HrxcG
//// RX Code for Group Call Channel ////

Group code number cannot be set since the 5-tone decoder
detects the other RX codes for a group code when the
received 5-tone contains one or more group code characters
(G or *).
#083
